+// Created by Dual contributors on 2026-10-23. Licensed under GPL-3.0; see the
+// LICENSE file.
+//
+// Dual on Linux: the two panes of a window are browser windows of their own
+// (each with its tabs, toolbar and address bar), placed side by side in one
+// shared window. This is the Linux counterpart of helium_dual_browser_mac.mm
+// and follows its rules (which pane opens where, hiding a pane, closing the
+// window, what is saved); what differs is the window itself. On macOS the
+// panes are windows of the window server kept over a frameless outer window.
+// Here they are windows of the outer window's own window tree (Aura), so
+// they move, resize, draw and are minimized with it, and this works the same
+// on X11 and on Wayland, where a program cannot place windows of its own.
